<title>NETHERLANDS: NEDCON OUT OF THE RED IN 1996.</title>
<headline>NEDCON OUT OF THE RED IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     4.48 vs   0.50 loss</p>
<p>    Net profit			     6.0  vs   0.7  loss</p>
<p>    Turnover			     115.1  vs  90.6</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     9.6  vs   0.2</p>
<p>    Cash flow				9.4  vs   2.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Warehouse equipment maker Nedcon Groep NV previously</p>
<p>said it expected the 1996 second half net profit to be at least</p>
<p>equal to the 1.3 million guilders posted in the first half of</p>
<p>the year.</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  1.50 vs   0.75</p>
<p>NOTE - Nedcon said the 1996 dividend could be taken up in</p>
<p>cash or in new Nedcon shares. Details of the optional stock</p>
<p>dividend will be published at a later date.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
